\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {21}{Every registered prediction, with the commit or registration that fixed it before the runs, its test, and its outcome. Labels are those of the registrations, except that the coherent-corruption and memory-probe predictions (registered as P1--P4 and P1--P3) are prefixed C and M. Failed predictions are tagged with the group used in Methods (Registrations): V, the value itself; C, an effect expected to carry over; P, the prompt, harness, reasoning or memory; D, the doubt detector.}}{15}{table.21}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces Held-out validation of the unprompted-doubt classifier: 100 runs not used in its development (60 without the concerns field, 40 under the registered prompt), labelled by an independent annotator blind to the classifier, whose answers were committed before labelling (commit 6964e2e). Cohen's $\kappa $ 0.90 (95\% bootstrap interval 0.80--0.98).}}{17}{table.22}\protected@file@percent }
